# --- Per-run working directories for the ChEBI identification method ----------
#
# The method is documented in CHEBI_IDENTIFICATION.md and its reusable parts live
# in structure_check/ and chebi_terms/. Everything one run produces is either a
# regenerable network cache or data derived from a single input spreadsheet, so
# none of it belongs in history: a finished run is a few MB of TSV answering a
# question nobody will ask again in that exact form.
#
# Written against mashroom*/ (the 2026-08 runs) and a generic chebi_run_*/ so a
# later batch can use either name.
mashroom*/
chebi_run_*/

# Bulk artifacts, in case a run directory is deliberately kept under another name.
**/.cache_pubchem.json
**/.cache_chebi.json
**/master.tsv
**/chebi_submission*.sdf

# Deliverables: communication artifacts addressed to ChEBI, the Lattice DB and
# the experimental team, with a date on them. Not source.
verified_chebi.tsv
unverified_chebi.tsv
chebi_submissions.tsv
lab_followup.tsv

# chebi_answer_ledger.tsv is the deliberate exception to all of the above. It is
# cumulative curation knowledge -- the answer for every compound identified so far,
# carried forward between batches -- and it is the one file here that cannot be
# regenerated: it embodies a round of questions to the experimental team and a
# correction that withdrew eight published identifiers. It is tracked on purpose.
#
# No rule above currently matches that name, so this negation is defensive rather
# than load-bearing: it is here so that broadening the deliverable rules to `*.tsv`
# cannot quietly stop tracking the one file that must never be lost.
!chebi_answer_ledger.tsv
